# Build output. esbuild writes compiled JS beside the HTML it belongs to, so
# the loadable extension is the package root and these are the parts of it that
# are generated.
#
# Every build path is anchored with a leading slash. Unanchored, `popup/` and
# `options/` match at any depth, so they also hid src/popup/ and src/options/ —
# the popup and options pages never reached the repo, and CI's build died on a
# source file that only ever existed on one laptop.
node_modules/
/background.js
/popup/
/options/
/dist/
/web-ext-artifacts/
